  ],
  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory\u00a0</em>for map 12 notes that the \"Via Claudia Augusta is the only named road known in the area of the map. It runs from the Po valley over\u00a0the Alps, into the Alpine foothills in Bavaria, and on to the Danube.\"</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Via Claudia Augusta was a Roman road that traversed the Alps, connecting the Po River valley to Rhaetia. Claudius began its construction in AD 46/7.",
